# Clean README

`README.md` is the public front door. Keep it durable product facts: what the SDK is, how to use it, where docs live.

## Put elsewhere

| Belongs in README | Belongs in `docs/releasing.md` (or nowhere) |
| --- | --- |
| Why it exists / what it does (can be one section) | Changesets, Version PRs, version hedges |
| Providers and drivers (definitions; catalog link last) | “Queued”, “until then”, `link:` / workspace paths |
| Install once published (`pnpm add …`) | Package matrices, npm readiness tables |

## Do not

- Keep a Status section that names products or duplicates the catalog link
- Narrate the release process (“first publish is queued via Changesets…”)
- Hedge versions (“expect `0.1.0`”) — versions come from package.json / npm
- Teach temporary local consumption unless the user asked for a contributor setup section
- Dump long code samples when the site docs already cover them — link to https://db-sdk.dev/docs instead
- Dump ADR process, agent notes, or changelog drafts into the README

## Example

```markdown
<!-- Bad -->
## Status
Postgres and Supabase ship today. [See what is available](https://db-sdk.dev/providers).

<!-- Good -->
## Providers and drivers
A driver is … A provider is … See ADR 0003 and the docs.

[See what is available](https://db-sdk.dev/providers).
```
